## How much do SEO content briefs cost?

The prices are fixed by volume:

- **One content brief:** £150
- **10 content briefs:** £1,200
- **25 content briefs:** £2,500

The 10-brief package works out at £120 per brief. The 25-brief package works out at £100 per brief.

Delivery is 2–3 working days per brief after the target and required inputs are confirmed. Batch timing depends on the number of briefs and is agreed before work begins.

## What is agreed before work begins?

Every brief needs a defined target. Before work starts we agree:

- the page topic and main search task
- whether the work is for a new page or an existing URL
- the intended reader and conversion goal
- the source material or product facts the writer must use
- the deliverables and delivery sequence
- how questions, feedback and revisions will be handled

We agree how revisions will be handled during scoping.

## How does the content brief process work?

The process has four stages.

1. **Confirm the target.** Share the topic, existing URL if there is one and the page goal.
2. **Review the search task.** Check the result types, recurring questions, content formats and realistic role for the page.
3. **Build the specification.** Set the heading sequence, evidence requirements, entity coverage, useful page elements and internal-link direction.
4. **Deliver the brief.** Receive the brief within 2–3 working days for the agreed item and route questions through the feedback approach agreed before work starts.

A brief does not guarantee rankings. Publication quality, source accuracy, site authority, implementation and competition still affect performance.

## Who are content briefs for?

Content briefs suit teams that already have writers but need stronger direction before drafting. They are useful when editors repeatedly need to restructure drafts, multiple writers need one standard or a topical plan is ready for production.

A single brief is a practical starting point if you want to test the format on one important page. A package suits an approved group of topics with enough writing capacity to use the briefs.

The service is less useful when the target page has not been chosen, business facts are unavailable or nobody owns the writing and review stage. Resolve those constraints before ordering a batch.

## Do content briefs include writing?

The listed prices cover the brief rather than the finished article. The writer uses the specification to create the draft.

If you need writing or another form of implementation then that work needs a separate scope. Agree the owner, source review and approval process before production starts.

## How do you request one content brief?

Send the target topic, the current page URL if one exists and a short description of the intended reader. Add any product facts, approved sources or internal pages that the writer must use.

One brief costs £150 and is delivered in 2–3 working days after the target and inputs are confirmed. Feedback and revision handling are agreed before work begins.

